# Bun releases

The build, installer, and update command agree on `{{project_slug}}-<os>-<arch>` and SHA256SUMS. Disable runtime configuration autoload in compiled binaries. Release targets each require a matching runner smoke test. If the application has native dependencies, include only the target's native package and test it on that platform.

Download into a temporary location, verify the checksum, and rename atomically beside the destination. Never modify a running binary in place. On checksum, network, or permission failures preserve the installed binary and clean temporary files. Source invocations cannot self-update. Release settings are independent of application config so invalid config cannot block repairs.

The workflow checks the tag against package version, runs check and build:all, verifies each binary's checksum and version on its OS/CPU, and publishes only after all smoke jobs pass. Only publishing receives contents-write. Extend smoke tests for optional application capabilities only when present.

Test release metadata, absent assets, checksums, permissions, path quoting, and atomic replacement using a local release server. Document `{{env_prefix}}_RELEASES_REPO`, `{{env_prefix}}_RELEASES_URL`, and `{{env_prefix}}_INSTALL_DIR`. Keep the installer working independently of optional apps.

Tests isolate `{{env_prefix}}_RELEASES_URL` to an unreachable local address unless they start a release stub. Assert broken application config cannot block `update`, checksum mismatch changes nothing, source mode refuses replacement, and a read-only install directory exits 6.
